# The packages of the Spark image that the Bronze decoder and the streaming job need, in spark/Dockerfile. `make lock-spark` writes requirements.txt with hashes.
# vitaldb decodes the publisher's case files. boto3 reads the landed object versions from S3 on the host. Both are the replay's pins.
vitaldb==1.7.2
boto3==1.43.126
# The streaming job: fastavro reads and writes the Avro wire bytes (the replay's pin). pyarrow and protobuf are what Spark 4.1.4's Python transformWithState
# needs, and protobuf is Spark's own pin (dev/requirements.txt of the 4.1.4 tag, the version of its generated code). Each was released at least two weeks before.
fastavro==1.13.1
pyarrow==26.0.1
protobuf==6.33.0
